# Public Reown/WalletConnect project identifier. Create one at cloud.reown.com
# and add the deployed site origin to the project's allowlist.
# Production builds do NOT read this file's real values from the Vercel
# dashboard (the CI token cannot read project env vars); the ci workflow
# injects them from GitHub repository secrets into web/.env.production.local
# before building. Keep secrets and .env.local in sync when rotating.
VITE_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID=replace-with-your-reown-project-id
# MapMonitor basemap overrides (all optional; the map defaults to
# OpenStreetMap with no key). Leave them unset for the default:
# https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png, attribution
# "© OpenStreetMap contributors", maxZoom 19.
# VITE_MAP_BASEMAP selects a registered basemap provider id (default `osm`;
# an unknown id falls back to `osm`).
# VITE_MAP_TILE_URL is a custom XYZ tile template using Leaflet's
# {z}/{x}/{y} placeholders. When set it defines a `custom` basemap and
# overrides VITE_MAP_BASEMAP.
# VITE_MAP_ATTRIBUTION is the attribution HTML/text the custom tile provider
# requires; Leaflet shows it in its attribution control.
# Copy real values into .env.local (gitignored) or Vercel env vars; never
# commit real keys here — this template file is tracked by git.
# VITE_MAP_BASEMAP=osm
# VITE_MAP_TILE_URL=https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png
# VITE_MAP_ATTRIBUTION=© OpenStreetMap contributors
